Commit:     John Bieling <john@thunderbird.net>
CommitDate: Sat Feb 8 22:57:38 2025 +0000

    Bug 1936378 - Reduce glitches while updating the message header area when tags and junk setting are changed simultaneously. r=aleca

    There seems to be a race between updating the tags in the UI, updating
    the junk status in the UI and the message being reloaded when the junk
    status changes.

    This patch moves the update of the junk status to the end, the message
    reload should then not interfere with the UI updates anymore. The patch
    also waits for the tag changes to be seen by a listener before updating
    the junk status.

    A tag update is also no longer removing/adding tags one by one. The
    missing tags and the obsolete tags are computed, and then added and
    removed at once.

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D237220

